# Target: core/broker_manager.py  (sync_all_balances ~337-355, + new _sync_ibkr)
# Opus trade-success-path audit 2026-05-29.
#
# CONFIRMED GAP:
#   sync_all_balances dispatches to _sync_alpaca / _sync_coinbase / _sync_kraken
#   (broker_manager.py:346-353) and falls through to "No sync handler" for
#   anything else. IBKR is the PREFERRED stock broker (trade_executor routes
#   stocks to IBKR when available) but has NO sync handler, so its real balance
#   is never pulled into broker_manager. get_broker_balance("ibkr") then returns
#   the {available: 0.0} default — which the per-broker cash check in
#   risk_manager.approve_trade (251-273) can read as "No available cash on ibkr"
#   and HARD-REJECT live IBKR entries. (See report-only R7 for the related
#   registration-state caveat — this diff only adds the handler, which is inert
#   unless 'ibkr' is a registered+enabled broker.)
#
# ibkr.get_account() already returns {equity, cash, buying_power, ...}
# (ibkr_executor.py:346-374). We reach the live singleton the same way diff 15
# does: core.trade_executor.executor._ibkr. Handler is wrapped in try/except and
# no-ops if IBKR is unavailable, so it is safe to add.
#
# NOTE (do not skip): registering 'ibkr'/'kraken' as default brokers is NOT in
# this diff. _register_defaults only runs on a FRESH install (_load_brokers
# restores persisted registrations otherwise), and it would require config key
# names I have not verified. See R7 — register once via register_broker() after
# confirming the persisted broker list and the kraken config var names.
--- a/core/broker_manager.py
